    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "No SDRF was found for this dataset, so each run was given a synthetic sample of its own. There is no sample metadata: treat every sample as unannotated."
   },
   {
    "code": "occupancy_not_stored",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Of 321185 occupancy entries MetaMorpheus wrote, some are not in ptm_stoichiometry: 3454 segment's accession not determinable from the sequences; 8565 site not in ptm_sites. 'site not in ptm_sites' means the entry's site has no ptm_sites row to key on; 'not determinable' means a cell's segments could not be assigned to its accessions from the sequences (QuantProject DEF-OCC-ACCESSION), which is never guessed. Absence of a row for these sites is therefore not NA. A 'duplicate' is a second entry for a (site, run) that already has a row: one with identical values loses nothing; one with DIFFERENT values means MetaMorpheus wrote two answers and the first in file order was stored (examples in bundle.json occupancy.differing_duplicates; which one should be stored is QuantProject's to define)."
   },
   {
    "code": "unplaced_ptm_sites",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "Some modifications on peptides shared between proteins were not written to ptm_sites for one or more of those proteins, because the peptide could not be located in that protein's sequence and the producer's residue spans cannot be paired with its accessions. Of the (PSM, protein) pairs affected: 2390 had no sequence in the searched databases; 2896 named a protein that does not contain the stored peptide -- typically a PSM ambiguous between peptide sequences (level 4 or 5), where this protein carries a different candidate than the first, which is the one stored; database(s) named by the search provenance but not on disk: F:\\aging_batch\\pxreprise-2eb9a52\\profiles\\lists\\MetaMorpheusContaminants_NoUPS.xml. Sites on the other proteins of the same PSMs are written. Counts are in bundle.json under protein_databases."
   },
   {
    "code": "unresolved_modifications",
    "severity": "warning",
    "message": "2 modification(s) could not be mapped to a UNIMOD accession or a mass, and are carried in ProForma as [Info:...] tags: Common Biological:Hydroxybutyrylation on K, UniProt:S-(2,3-dicarboxypropyl)cysteine on C. Their ptm_sites rows exist and carry modification_name, with modification null, so a query by name finds them and a query by UNIMOD accession will not."
   },
   {
    "code": "collapsed_duplicate_rows",
    "severity": "info",
    "message": "The producer wrote some rows more than once, identical in every column, and the copies were dropped so each identifier appears once. Nothing was lost: the kept row is byte-for-byte what the duplicates said. Rows that share an identifier and disagree anywhere are still refused rather than collapsed. protein_groups: 7 identifier(s), 10 row(s) dropped, e.g. PXD038328:C0HKD1;C0HKD2;C0HKD3;D3YZF6 written 4 times; quant_values: 281 identifier(s), 402 row(s) dropped, e.g. PXD038328:20221108_E1_LS01_Serena_acetylom_A19:label_free:protein_group:PXD038328:C0HKD1;C0HKD2;C0HKD3;D3YZF6:QuantProject:DEF-PROT-SPC written 4 times. The full list is in bundle.json under collapsed_duplicates."
   },
